# Admin saving indicator (required)

Whenever Admin code **saves, deletes, or applies** data that may take more than a moment, show the shared waiting overlay — do **not** rely on inline text alone.

## Standard pattern

Use `AdminLoading.withSaving()` (preferred) or `withAdminBusy(fn, { saving: true, supportMessage: "…" })` from `js/admin.js`:

```javascript
return global.AdminLoading.withSaving(async () => {
  // set local saving flags, rerender if needed, await network/DB work
}, {
  key: "unique-operation-key",
  supportMessage: "Saving feature…" // optional detail under the main message
});
```

## Messages

- **Loading / fetching:** `BrandLoading.CANONICAL_MESSAGE` → `"Hang tight! Just getting your info."`
- **Saving / deleting / applying:** `BrandLoading.SAVING_MESSAGE` → `"Hang tight! Saving your info."`

The overlay is the animated nine-square logo from `brand-loading.css` / `admin-loading.js`.

## When to use

- Explicit Save / Create / Delete / Apply buttons
- Multi-step writes (e.g. feature + class templates + ships)
- Any async persist that replaces DOM or navigates away

## When inline-only is OK

- Quiet background autosave (`quiet: true`) — button/status text is enough
- Instant client-only state (tab switch, form draft) with no network call

## New modules

Standalone admin modules loaded before `admin.js` should call `global.AdminLoading.withSaving` directly (see `withSavingOverlay` helpers in cruise-line features, stateroom types, ports, media library).
